    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116">

                <pb facs="0210" n="864" sameAs="frus:frus1875v02/pg864"/>

                <head>No. 415.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-02-08"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 8,
                        1875</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 188.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I enclose herewith a copy of a letter of
                    the 5th instant from the Secretary of War, accompanied by one of a report of the
                    commanding officer of Fort Duncan, Texas, by which it appears that the officer
                    in command of the Mexican forces in Northern Coahuila has been instructed to
                    fight Indians hostile to this country, and to co-operate with United States
                    troops when requested to do so.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to express to the Mexican Government the gratification of this
                    Department that such orders have been issued.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d116-a1.xml" xpointer="d116-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d116-a2.xml" xpointer="d116-a2"/>
